KaTeX 0.17.0 — vendored.

Source: the 1.0 tree at /home/deploy/dev/cadus/static/vendor/katex, copied byte for byte.
Files: katex.min.js (UMD), auto-render.min.js (the extension), katex.min.css, fonts/*.woff2
(woff2 only — the npm package also ships woff and ttf, 1.5 MB against 600 KB).

Why this tree and not the npm package (spec section 4.3):

- index.html loads the two scripts as UMD globals, katex.min.js FIRST. auto-render reads
  `katex.ParseError` at load; the reverse order captures `undefined`, every render throws,
  and every problem prints raw LaTeX.
- The stylesheet stays a <link> to this tree, ahead of the app bundle, so the app's
  `.problem-text .katex` override keeps the cascade.
- The files sit under `public/`, so Vite copies them verbatim. A build never rewrites,
  hashes, or inlines them, and `font-src 'self'` (no `data:`) stays satisfied.

Do not edit these files. To move to another KaTeX release, replace the whole directory.
